<div class="mb-10"><h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Benchmarks: Soli vs Ruby</h1>
<p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-6">Reproducible per-operation numbers comparing Soli's production engine against Ruby. The scripts ship in <code class="text-cyan-400">bench/cross-language/</code> so you can re-run them yourself.</p>
<div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/5 p-5 mb-8"><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-amber-400">Read this first.</strong> Benchmarks are easy to rig and easy to get wrong &mdash; this page has already been corrected once (see <a href="#corrections" class="text-amber-400 hover:underline">Corrections</a>). Everything below is best-of-7 on <strong class="text-white">byte-identical inputs</strong> generated by the same LCG in both languages, and Ruby is credited with its <strong class="text-white">best</strong> result across three modes, not its slowest. Where Soli loses, the number is printed exactly as measured.</p></div></div>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Setup</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 mb-6"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><tbody class="text-gray-400 divide-y divide-white/10">
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-medium w-32">Soli</td><td class="py-3 px-4">production bytecode VM (<code class="text-cyan-400">soli --vm</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-medium w-32">Ruby</td><td class="py-3 px-4">4.0.6 &mdash; default, <code class="text-cyan-400">--yjit</code>, <code class="text-cyan-400">--zjit</code></td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-medium w-32">Method</td><td class="py-3 px-4">best-of-7 per operation, warmed once first</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-medium w-32">Data</td><td class="py-3 px-4">n = 20,000; identical LCG-generated inputs in both languages</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-medium w-32">Machine</td><td class="py-3 px-4">idle 16-core x86-64 Linux</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="text-gray-400 mb-8"><strong class="text-white">ratio</strong> is Soli &divide; Ruby's <em>best</em> mode. <strong class="text-amber-400">Below 1.00 means Soli is faster.</strong></p>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Summary</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 mb-6"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-300"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4">Category</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">Geometric mean</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">Soli wins</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-gray-400 divide-y divide-white/10">
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white">String</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400">0.36&times; &mdash; Soli <strong>2.8&times; faster</strong></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">11/13</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white">Array</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-amber-300">1.15&times; &mdash; Ruby 1.1&times; faster</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">7/16</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white">DateTime</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-amber-300">2.54&times; &mdash; Ruby 2.5&times; faster</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1/9</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white">Hash</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-amber-300">2.18&times; &mdash; Ruby 2.2&times; faster</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1/11</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white">Duration</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-amber-300">9.08&times; &mdash; Ruby 9.1&times; faster</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0/2</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white">Numeric</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-amber-300">3.83&times; &mdash; Ruby 3.8&times; faster</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0/3</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white">Control</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-amber-300">3.80&times; &mdash; Ruby 3.8&times; faster</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0/2</td></tr>
<tr class="bg-white/5"><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-bold">Overall</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-white font-bold">1.36&times;</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-white font-bold">20/56</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">Soli is ahead on <strong class="text-white">20 of 56</strong> operations but behind on the geometric mean. The split tracks <em>where the work happens</em>:</p>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-400 space-y-2 mb-8"><li><strong class="text-emerald-400">Inside Rust</strong> (string transforms, <code class="text-cyan-400">flatten</code>, <code class="text-cyan-400">union</code>, <code class="text-cyan-400">sort</code>, <code class="text-cyan-400">DateTime.parse</code>) &mdash; Soli wins, often by 3&ndash;30&times;.</li><li><strong class="text-amber-300">Per-element in interpreted code</strong> (arithmetic loops, function calls, blocks, hash iteration) &mdash; Ruby wins by 2&ndash;6&times;.</li></ul>
<p class="text-gray-400 mb-10">If your hot path transforms data with built-in methods, Soli is faster. If it is a tight hand-written loop, Ruby's JIT is faster.</p>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">String</h2><p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">Soli's strings are Rust <code class="text-cyan-400">EcoString</code>s and the methods are native code with no per-element interpretation. Soli's strongest category.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 mb-10"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-300"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4">Operation</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">Soli</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">Ruby</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">+YJIT</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">+ZJIT</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">Ratio</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-gray-400 divide-y divide-white/10">
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">capitalize</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.020</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.281</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.284</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.302</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">0.07&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">downcase</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.004</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.035</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.035</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.034</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">0.11&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">upcase</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.004</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.029</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.030</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.034</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">0.14&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">replace_all</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.082</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.457</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.464</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.459</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">0.18&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">contains</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.003</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.014</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.014</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.013</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">0.20&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">concat_plus</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.362</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">4.885</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">5.439</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">5.243</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">0.28&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">bytes</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.145</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.408</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.433</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.435</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">0.35&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">chars</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.143</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">2.783</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">2.693</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">2.867</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">0.42&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">sub</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.002</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.006</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.005</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.006</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">0.52&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">split</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.240</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.288</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.280</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.281</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">0.86&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">index_of</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.011</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.014</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.014</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.013</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">0.85&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">interpolate</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.814</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.539</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.569</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.584</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">1.18&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">reverse</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.062</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.018</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.018</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.018</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">3.56&times;</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Array</h2><p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">Mixed. Soli wins the bulk native transforms (<code class="text-cyan-400">flatten</code>, <code class="text-cyan-400">union</code>, <code class="text-cyan-400">sort</code>, <code class="text-cyan-400">join</code>); Ruby wins anything calling a block per element, and the set operations on partially-overlapping data.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 mb-10"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-300"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4">Operation</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">Soli</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">Ruby</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">+YJIT</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">+ZJIT</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">Ratio</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-gray-400 divide-y divide-white/10">
