<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">filter</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.323</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.676</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.591</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.684</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">2.24&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">build</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">2.608</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.489</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.485</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.480</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">0.75&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">each</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.109</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.536</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.475</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.498</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">2.34&times;</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">DateTime</h2><p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">One enormous Soli win (<code class="text-cyan-400">parse</code> at 29&times; &mdash; Ruby's <code class="text-cyan-400">Time.parse</code> is famously slow) against consistent losses elsewhere. Every Soli DateTime operation allocates an object; Ruby's <code class="text-cyan-400">Time</code> arithmetic mostly does not.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 mb-10"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-300"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4">Operation</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">Soli</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">Ruby</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">+YJIT</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">+ZJIT</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">Ratio</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-gray-400 divide-y divide-white/10">
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">parse</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">4.542</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">158.033</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">139.985</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">146.613</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">0.03&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">format</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">7.258</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">6.334</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">6.046</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">6.132</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">1.20&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">now</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">5.134</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.227</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.121</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.137</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">4.58&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">subtract_days</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.465</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.828</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.861</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.786</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">4.41&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">add_hours</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.497</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.829</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.828</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.776</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">4.51&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">end_of_month</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">9.686</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">2.033</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.868</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.822</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">5.31&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">from_unix</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.904</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.749</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.687</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.702</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">5.68&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">to_unix</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">2.179</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.422</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.432</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.422</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">5.17&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">year</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.258</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.429</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.414</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.414</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">7.88&times;</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Hash</h2><p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">Ruby leads across the board. Both use open-addressing maps with fast hashers, so the gap is not the data structure &mdash; it is the per-iteration interpreter cost around it.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 mb-10"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-300"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4">Operation</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">Soli</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">Ruby</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">+YJIT</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">+ZJIT</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">Ratio</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-gray-400 divide-y divide-white/10">
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">build</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">2.674</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.466</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.480</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">3.469</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">0.77&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">merge</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.731</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.731</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.739</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.710</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">1.03&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">set</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.159</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.094</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.131</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.069</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">1.08&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">has_key</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.049</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.110</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.086</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.041</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">1.01&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">get</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.126</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.970</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.942</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.830</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">1.36&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">invert</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.783</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.469</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.439</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.437</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">1.79&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">each</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.089</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.519</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.466</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.502</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">2.34&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">transform_values</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1.648</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.563</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.510</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.566</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">3.23&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">select</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">2.108</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.663</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.813</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">0.570</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">3.70&times;</td></tr>
